--- the Omega_p obstruction (why p^{-2}M_2 is not assembled here) ---
BK p. 272: Ehat = Gm-hat over W via eta_p(t) = exp[Omega_p^{-1} lambda(t)] - 1,
with Omega_p in W^x a p-adic period.  For E/Q ordinary at p the Galois action
on T_p(Ehat) is the cyclotomic character times the unramified character sending
Frobenius to alpha^{-1}, so Frob(Omega_p)/Omega_p = alpha^{+-1}.  A solution of
Frob(X) = cX with c in Z_p^x lies in W(F_{p^d})/p^N only if c^d = 1 mod p^N.
The lines above show alpha^(p-1) != 1, so Omega_p lies in no finite unramified
extension of Z_p; and the criterion class divides by p^2, so the assembly needs
Omega_p mod p^3, hence unramified degree ord(alpha) in (Z/p^3)^x -- the last
column above -- on top of the ramified Z_p[zeta_p] the level-p Fourier
resolution of the Teichmueller twists needs.  That is the blocker.

